    "name": "tokyo-night",
    "note": "Tokyo Night (VS Code enkia.tokyo-night 1.1.2): dark is 'Tokyo Night Storm', light is 'Tokyo Night Light' (the extension's one light theme, the 'regular' light). Light takes the VS Code theme's own deep, muted palette, its terminal included. Dark takes Storm's surface and the Tokyo Night palette as kitty ships it (folke's tokyonight_storm: green #9ECE6A, where the VS Code terminal has the teal #73DACA for green beside a cyan, two colours a glyph could not tell apart). Departures, each for a rule of the shell: the muted text is a greyer ink than the source's blue-grey (#5E606C / #A9AEC0), which sat within a glyph's distance of the blue and the magenta, so an off glyph read as on; dark's bright cyan (color14) is the teal #73DACA and its faint text #5F6894 (2.7:1; the comment colour is 2.35:1); light's spill and bright yellow (color11) are the ochre #9A7A2C, apart from the orange. Group tabs: the tab is the orange, a locked group's tab the teal. btop: the stock tokyo-storm in dark, custom in light.",
